      "writtenOn": "2017-01-30T22:33:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks to me like this Link method relies on p.hashResult being computed correctly before it gets run, which is currently done in the Compile method.\n\nCan we check that p.hashResult is non-null (unless ioutil already does that)?\n\nAlternatively we could move hashResult (and potentially the other changing fields, such as compiled, failed, and rebuilt) out of the GoPackage data structure and make it a parameter of the Compile and of the Link methods (and have it be computed in another method) to make it super clear that it needs to be computed beforehand (this seems like the cleanest approach to me although I suspect this is more work than we want).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 239,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "7768148bea4bc87dd6c0acf486028ed9aef8e71e",
